<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Mukhtar al-Thaqafi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 622–687</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Mukhtar al-Thaqafi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Mukhtar al-Thaqafi was an Arab revolutionary who seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kufa">Kufa</a> in 685 in the name of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya, a son of Ali, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a>. He took revenge on the killers of Husayn and won support from non-Arab converts, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mawali">mawali</a>. His army defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyads</a> on the Khazir River in 686, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musab-ibn-al-zubayr">Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr</a> besieged him in Kufa, where he was killed in 687.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-mukhtar-al-thaqafi.jpg" alt="al-Mukhtar al-Thaqafi" width="320" height="466" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PRINCE FORCECR · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jpg.%D9%84%D9%88%D8%AD%D8%A9%D9%80%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%AE%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1_%D9%80%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AB%D9%82%D9%81%D9%8A.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
